  note    = {Compiles LEXICALLY-scoped effect handlers to code with no residual overhead when the
             continuation is not captured — the compilation payoff of the Q27 resumption-grade
             thesis, realized. The seam bang wants: when a handler is tail-resumptive / one-shot
             the compiler emits a plain call+return (no continuation reification), reserving the
             expensive resumable-closure path for the genuinely multi-shot case. Lexical scoping
             (the cap names its lexically-enclosing handler) is EXACTLY bang's identity-dispatch
             semantics (ADR-0054: typing by label, dispatch by identity = lexical). Evidence that
             the empty-ω-channel optimization (Q27's compiler seam) is a real, measured technique,
             not a hypothesis. Assessed in docs/notes/multishot-survey.md §grades.},
}

