  note    = {The performer-side compilation story: an EVIDENCE VECTOR (one entry per effect in the row,
             pushed down the evaluation context) turns `perform op` from a stack SEARCH for the innermost
             handler into a LOCAL O(1) lookup (Sec 2.5, 3.1) — the single `perform` rule's two costs
             (Searching + Capturing) are split, and evidence kills the search. Canonical (constant-time
             lookup, Koka's choice) vs insertion-ordered (cheap to build, linear lookup) vectors, Sec 2.5.
             Tail-resumptive ops evaluate IN-PLACE, avoiding the yield/resume cycle entirely. The STATIC
             analogue of bang's identity-keyed dispatch: bang types by LABEL / dispatches by IDENTITY at
             runtime via `splitAtId` (a search); where the row is concrete, the same evidence-vector move
             would replace that search — assessed in docs/notes/calculated-typer-survey.md §c. Row-typed
             framework required (evidence shape = the row).},
}

