            Key method: a SYMBOLIC MUTATION strategy -- drop a hypothesis from a proven
            theorem (H1 -> H2 -> C), use the Lean prover to confirm the dropped hypothesis was
            NECESSARY, yielding a false mutated_version (a counterexample target) plus a
            dropped_hypothesis necessity obligation; multi-reward expert iteration over both.
            Directly informs our gap 1 (automated counterexample search; cf. Surface's
            test/StackVal idiom) AND gap 3 (hypothesis-necessity / non-vacuity testing) --
